    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e0049b2_f828f1ea",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/man.go",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 354,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-13T20:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it could loop forever if m.Cache.Delete kept returning errors. The spec suggests to remove token certs whenever possible, so I wanted to make sure we do that.\n\nThis method is always called from a separate goroutine, though, so it won\u0027t block other things.\nAdded a doc comment to clarify.",
      "parentUuid": "3e3be95b_d49a7c6e",
      "revId": "5a7a9287c3f5c7c6b80d4cadf78e815a6509d75e",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e3be95b_8f1701a3",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/man.go",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 354,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-13T22:13:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still don\u0027t think it should loop forever. If a Cache.Delete fails, it\u0027s pretty likely it\u0027s going to fail again.",
      "parentUuid": "3e0049b2_f828f1ea",
      "revId": "5a7a9287c3f5c7c6b80d4cadf78e815a6509d75e",
